---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';

// Final text v3, approved 2026-11-17 after two review rounds. Use it word for word; change it only with Christian's
// approval.
const email = site.contactEmail;
---

<Layout title="terms" description="The terms for using Cueory." noindex>
  <Prose>
    <h1>terms of use</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft">Last updated: 17 November 2026</p>

    <p>By using Cueory you agree to these terms. If you don't agree, please don't use the site.</p>

    <p>
      <strong>Who we are.</strong> Cueory is an independent study site for nursing students, owned and run by an
      individual in Arizona, USA. In these terms, "Cueory", "we" and "us" mean that owner. You can reach us at
      <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>Who can use Cueory.</strong> Cueory is for nursing students and is not aimed at children. You must be at
      least 13. We don't knowingly collect information from anyone under 13; if we learn we have, we delete it. Parents
      can email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> to have a child's information deleted. If you're 13 to 17, a
      parent or guardian must read and agree to these terms for you.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>What Cueory is today.</strong> Cueory is still being built. Right now it has daily puzzles and some sample
      or placeholder study pages. Real lessons and practice questions are added as they're ready. Cueory is a study aid
      only, so please read our <a href="/disclaimer">disclaimer</a>.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>Free to use.</strong> Cueory is free to use right now. If that ever changes, we'll say so here first. We
      may change, pause or stop any part of Cueory at any time.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>Changes to these terms.</strong> We may update these terms. We'll post the new version here with a new
      date, and for important changes we'll show a notice on the site for at least 14 days. Important changes apply 14
      days after we post the notice; other changes apply when posted. Changes never apply to disputes that started
      earlier. If you don't agree with a change, please stop using Cueory.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>Accounts.</strong> Accounts are optional and not open yet. When they open, keep your sign-in details to
      yourself. You'll be able to delete your account at any time on the account page.
    </p>

    <p><strong>Using it fairly.</strong> Please don't:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>copy, sell or republish our lessons, questions, puzzles or design without our written permission;</li>
      <li>share real exam or test questions from your school or any licensing exam;</li>
      <li>try to break, overload or get around the site's security;</li>
      <li>scrape the site or use bots to collect its content;</li>
      <li>send us anything illegal or harmful, or anyone's private information, including patient information.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We may block or limit anyone who breaks these terms.</p>

    <p>
      <strong>Our content.</strong> The lessons, questions, puzzles, the cueory name and logo, and the site's design
      belong to Cueory or to those who license them to us. You may use them for your own personal, non-commercial study.
      We keep all other rights.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>Your feedback.</strong> If you send us a flag, comment or idea, by email or later through the "Flag or
      comment" button, we may use it to improve Cueory. We won't owe you payment for it. Our
      <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a> explains what we keep.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>Copyright concerns.</strong> If you think something on Cueory copies your work, email
      <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> with what the work is, where it appears on Cueory, your contact details,
      and a statement that you own it or act for the owner. We'll look into it and remove it if needed.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>Other services.</strong> Some parts of Cueory link to or use services we don't run: Kit for launch-update
      emails, Ko-fi for optional tips, YouTube for videos, Google for sign-in once accounts open, and our social media
      pages. Their own terms and privacy policies apply when you use them. Tips through Ko-fi are optional. A tip doesn't
      buy you anything and doesn't change what you can use. Refunds follow Ko-fi's rules.
    </p>

    <p><strong>Your privacy.</strong> Our <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a> explains what we keep and why.</p>

    <p>
      <strong>No warranty.</strong> Cueory is provided "as is" and "as available". <strong>To the fullest extent the law
      allows, we make no warranties of any kind, express or implied, including implied warranties of merchantability,
      fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement.</strong> We don't promise the site will be accurate,
      complete, up to date, uninterrupted, secure or free of errors. You use Cueory, and rely on its content, at your own
      risk.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>Limit of liability.</strong> <strong>To the fullest extent the law allows, Cueory and anyone who helps run
      it are not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential or punitive losses, or for lost data, grades,
      exam results or income. For anything else, our total liability to you is limited to US $50.</strong> Some places
      don't allow some of these limits, so parts of this may not apply to you. Nothing here limits liability that the law
      says can't be limited.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>The whole agreement.</strong> These terms, the <a href="/disclaimer">disclaimer</a> and the
      <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a> are the whole agreement between you and Cueory. If a court finds part of them
      can't be enforced, the rest still applies. If we don't enforce a term right away, we can still enforce it later.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>Law.</strong> Arizona law (USA) applies to these terms, without regard to its conflict-of-law rules. Any
      dispute will be handled in the state or federal courts located in Maricopa County, Arizona, unless the law where
      you live gives you a right that can't be waived.
    </p>

    <p><strong>Contact.</strong> Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.</p>
  </Prose>
</Layout>
